# Rotation for the two service logs that bypass the journal.
#
# universal-chess.service and universal-chess-web.service redirect their output
# straight at these files with StandardOutput=append:, so nothing bounds their
# size but this config. Boards run for weeks on an SD card with a small /var.
#
# copytruncate is required, not a preference: systemd opens the redirect target
# once and holds that descriptor for the lifetime of the service. Renaming the
# file -- what logrotate does by default -- would leave the running service
# writing into the rotated file while the new one stayed empty, so logging would
# silently stop until the next restart. Truncating keeps the inode, and because
# the descriptor is opened O_APPEND the next write resumes at offset zero.

/var/log/modmenuoutput.log
/var/log/universal-chess-web.log
{
    daily
    rotate 3
    maxsize 10M
    copytruncate
    compress
    delaycompress
    missingok
    notifempty
}
